      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "title": "READ ME",
      "widgets_values": [
        "StereoForge v2 - layered depth stereo\n\nInput = left eye, copied bit-exactly. The right eye is rendered at full resolution from the ORIGINAL pixels using Depth Anything 3 depth.\n\nFloor reflections (puddles, wet floors): the reflector is segmented, the floor plane fitted, and the reflected image is moved at its mirrored (virtual) depth while the floor and puddle outline move with the surface. Fresnel reflectance decides how much of each pixel is reflection, so texture seen through shallow water stays on the floor.\n\nparallax 3% = nearest content gets 3% of the width. metric_ipd + 65 = physically scaled (orthostereo) with the metric DA3 model.\nBypass the Reflector Mask node for scenes without reflections."
      ]
    }
